A||N||1||Gene Hilston||87 GT  temp gage faulty??? HELP||||5||
Z||000000||Gene Hilston||06-19-2000||02:37 AM||||Temperature gauge keeps jumping back and forth between 170 and passed 260 wich then triggers my overheating warning light to come on.  No sign of overheating.  had radiator and engine flushed and filled.  New thermostat installed.  When cruising down the highway it stays at 220 for about 1 minute or so then goes to passed 260, stays there for about 3 minutes then returns to 220 then back again!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-19-2000||09:03 AM||||You need to "burp" the system you have an air pocket in the system. The easiest way to get it out is raise the back of the car, Open the front radiator cap SLOWLY. When coolant starts to leak close cap. Open cap on thermostat housing in back and remove thermostat. It will most likely be low. Just fill it up with a 50/50 mix of coolant and water. Your problem should go away.||||reg||1
